course: dictionary
lesson: 10141
title: Thrillers and thrills
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thriller is an exciting book, film or TV show full of suspense and danger. It keeps you wanting to know what happens next. The word comes from thrill, the tingly feeling of excitement inside you.
explain: Context tells you what a word means. «Michael Jackson's album Thriller, from 1982, is widely reported as the best-selling album of all time, usually estimated at around 70 million copies, not a billion.» Words like album, copies and best-selling show that Thriller is a music album here, not a story.
explain: The word can also be used in sport. When a match is close and exciting until the very end, people call it a thriller. The sentence around the word shows which meaning is meant, so read the clues before you decide.
fact: A thriller is a noun. Its plural is thrillers.
fact: Thrillers often have cliffhangers, a ticking clock, twists and a hero in danger.
fact: Crime thrillers, spy thrillers and chase thrillers are common types of story.
fact: In informal talk, «a real thriller» means a very exciting event, like a match that stays close until the end.
fact: The album «Thriller» is a name, so it starts with a capital letter.
exercise: «The detective read a crime thriller on the train.» What is a thriller in this sentence? | A shop that sells maps | A type of train | *A book full of suspense and crime | A kind of cake
exercise: «The match was a real thriller, with the winning goal in the last minute.» What does thriller mean here? | A film about spies | A boring, empty stadium | *An exciting, close game | A rainy day
exercise: Which feature is typical of a thriller? | A list of shopping | *A ticking clock | A long nap | A happy ending with no danger at all
test: «Michael Jackson's album Thriller, from 1982, is widely reported as the best-selling album of all time.» Why does Thriller have a capital letter here? | It means very exciting | It is the name of a sport | It starts a sentence about a crime | *It is the name of an album
test: Which word in the sentence tells you Thriller is an album and not a story? | estimated | billion | 1982 | *album
exam: Sam says a thriller must always be about a spy. Is Sam right? | No, a thriller is a cookbook | Yes, thrillers are always about trains | Yes, spies are the only thrillers | *No, a thriller can be a crime, spy or chase story, or a close sports match
